    "title": "# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design",
    "text": "**Status: in progress — Phase 0.1.** Moved up from `Aperas-design.md`'s originally-speculative\nPhase 4 slot: the roadmap item's stated precondition — \"confirming that TerminusDB Community\nedition's rough edges... are structural rather than incidental before committing engineering\neffort to a replacement\" — is resolved by this session's live-verified findings ([§2](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/2. What confirmed this isn't incidental]]>)), and the\nswitch itself has been decided. This doc is the concrete engine, storage encoding, and query model\nfor that work, not a still-open proposal.",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CBFDW940000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG002",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG003",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG009",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG00V",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 1. The actual reason, stated first, not derived from a benchmark",
    "text": "This is not a response to a measured bottleneck — the production access pattern this project\nactually uses today (bulk tree fetch via `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL`) is fast, ~18ms for a\n91-node tree (`Aperas-kg-foundational-design.md` §2's benchmark table — where ApeironNgn's own\nnumber, 5.6ms for the same tree post-rehydration, also now lives). The reason is architectural fit\nwith Aperas's own stated philosophy\n(`Aperas-design.md`'s \"Metaphysical foundation,\" `Aperas-kg-foundational-design.md` §1): a boundary\nagent is supposed to \"sample the fluid core (Apeiron) and project it into rigid, type-safe\nstructures (Peras).\" TerminusDB forces that projection to happen *twice*, redundantly and\ninconsistently — once into TerminusDB's own JSON-LD schema (a Peras TerminusDB owns), and again\ninto whatever shape each of WOQL/GraphQL/the Document API happens to hand back (three different\nPerata for the identical `source`/`target` fields, live-verified: plain string, plain-string-with-\nwrapped-literals, and a full-IRI-bearing nested object, respectively). ApeironNgn's actual promise\nis collapsing that to one Peras: the OOP class *is* the schema and *is* the traversal mechanism,\nso there's no second, independent projection layer for the query language to disagree with the\nclass about. \"Form is not a rigid cage, but a temporary, playful instrument\" (`Aperas-design.md`)\n— a class boundary the application itself owns is exactly that; a schema language plus three\nindependently-shaped query surfaces on top of it is the opposite.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG003:props:StringProp:00CBFDYXN8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
