  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMG00Y",
    "text": "**Storage: in-memory only, deliberately, for now.** Checked live (`oxigraph` skill,\n     `references/persistence.md`): the Node/WASM build has no RocksDB, no on-disk option at all —\n     `Store` is pure in-process memory, rehydrated from `AperasKG/Apeiron/`'s JSON-LD at process\n     start (`store.ts`'s `rehydrateStore`). Decided: stay here rather than reach for `pyoxigraph`\n     (native, RocksDB-backed, but a second language/process needing its own projection bridge to\n     the Node UI) or a native non-WASM Node binding (real engineering work of its own) — revisit\n     only once the KG's actual size makes in-memory rehydration or working-set size a real problem\n     (GB-level), not before. No separate JS-level cache on top of it, for the same reason — one\n     memory tier, not two, kept simple until something actually demands otherwise.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG00X",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
