    "title": "00CBFDYXMG00Z",
    "text": "**The prop-access interface.** [§3](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/3. The concrete design]]>)'s `a.b.c` traversal (`node.ts`'s `wrapNode`) — see [§3](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/3. The concrete design]]>)'s\n     updated note on why this ended up as a plain per-node `Proxy` rather than the Gremlin-\n     isomorphic deferred-execution model originally sketched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG00X",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMG010",
    "text": "**The `export.ts`/`Link` gap — fixed and live-verified, not just noted.** `INSTANCE_CLASSES`\n     now includes `Link`; `apeironNgn/store.ts`'s `INSTANCE_FILES` reads it too, so a `Link`'s own\n     `target`/`predicate` rehydrate correctly instead of leaving a dangling reference. The fix\n     needed more than adding a name to a list: `BlockNode` and `Link` form a genuine two-way\n     reference cycle (`BlockNode.links` -> `Link` id, `Link.target` -> a `BlockNode` id — the same\n     cycle `crud.ts`'s `findLinkIdsTargeting` already documents for deletion), and TerminusDB\n     checks referential integrity per commit, not across commits — live-verified: a `BlockNode`\n     referencing a not-yet-existing `Link` id fails even when that `Link` is created in the very\n     next separate call, but succeeds when both are submitted together in one commit, in either\n     order. `importJsonLd` now commits `BlockNode`+`Link` together as one group\n     (`IMPORT_COMMIT_GROUPS`) rather than as two separate per-class calls. Round-trip verified live:\n     created a real embedded-literal `Link` (server-assigned id, same shape `artifacts.ts`'s\n     `resolveBlockLinks` produces in normal use) referencing a target `BlockNode`, exported it,\n     deleted both from TerminusDB, re-imported from the mirror, and confirmed both documents came\n     back at their original ids with the reference intact in both directions.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG00X",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
