    "title": "00CBFDYXMG02M",
    "text": "`treeChildren` → `this.root ? [this.root] : []` (unchanged — still what rendering/`kg:tree` see).\n    `findChild`/`appendChild` as originally built here matched/attached against `root` itself as a\n    single opaque child, `appendChild` throwing once a root already existed; [§4](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/4. Rollout sequence]]>) [Step 6](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/4. Rollout sequence/Step 6: ingest ordering, `--track`, link-resolution reporting, and root-document addressing — implemented, verified]]>) replaced both\n    with the current behavior (delegate through to the root document, root and artifact addressed as\n    one logical node) — see [Step 6](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/4. Rollout sequence/Step 6: ingest ordering, `--track`, link-resolution reporting, and root-document addressing — implemented, verified]]>) for why and the mechanics.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG02K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG02N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMG02N",
    "text": "`project.ts`'s `projectArtifactToMarkdown`'s render half → `node.toMarkdown()` (frontmatter via\n    `withFrontmatter` plus `this.root.toMarkdown()`; `null` when there's no root yet).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG02K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG02P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMG02P",
    "text": "`artifacts.ts`'s `trackArtifact`'s per-node half → `node.trackFromDisk(artifactPath)` — takes\n    the path explicitly (not `this.path`), since a brand-new, not-yet-tracked instance has no path\n    of its own yet. Folding this onto the class turned out to remove real duplication: the old\n    free function needed separate \"new node\" (mint an `artifactId`, set every field) and \"existing\n    node\" (check the hash, maybe skip, set every field) branches; once `key` replaced the separate\n    `artifactId` field, there's nothing left to mint, so one method body now handles both — a\n    fresh node's `fileHash` just reads `undefined`, unconditionally \"changed.\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG02K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG02Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMG02Q",
    "text": "`artifacts.ts`'s `ingestArtifact`'s per-node half → `node.ingestFromDisk()`, returning\n    `{ blockCount, reconciliation, pendingLinks }`. Deliberately does *not* also resolve the\n    `pendingLinks` itself — that's `artifacts.ts`'s `resolveBlockLinks`, a multi-block sweep with\n    no single node to be `this`, run by the free `ingestArtifact` wrapper immediately after.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG02K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
