    ],
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR01S",
    "text": "`node.ts`: `Link` gains `declare props?: ApeironNode[]`. `BaseNode` gains `addWikilink(target,\n  positions)` — mints one fresh `Link` (predicate `WIKILINK_PREDICATE`), sets its `props` to one\n  `{key: 'position', value: '<offset>'}` entry per position, and attaches it by id. A dedicated\n  method, not an overload of `addLink` (which `kg:link` also calls, with no position or\n  dedup-by-target concept of its own) — and, necessarily, back to the \"mint id, `wrap()`, set\n  fields, attach by id\" shape `addLink`'s own doc comment says `links` becoming `storageKind:\n  'embed'` retired: `mintEmbedded` only writes an entry's own top-level fields, it doesn't recurse\n  into a nested `Set`-typed one, so a single-call `{predicate, target, props}` literal can't mint\n  `props` correctly — safe to always mint fresh here (never merge into an existing same-target\n  `Link`) since every wikilink-derived `Link` on a block is already stripped before this runs\n  ([Step 7](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/4. Rollout sequence/Step 7: `ArtifactNode extends BlockNode`, the root block retired outright, `text` a copied abstract for both — implemented, verified]]>)'s `hydrateFromParsed` fix). (Superseded by [Step 9](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/4. Rollout sequence/Step 9: consistent tombstoning (incl. recursive artifact removal) and wikilink `Link` identity stability — implemented, verified]]>): `addWikilink` split into a\n  non-attaching `mintWikilink`, and `hydrateFromParsed` no longer strips wikilinks up front — the\n  \"always mint fresh, nothing to reuse\" premise here no longer holds.)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR01T",
    "text": "`astParser.ts`: `sliceWithOffset`/`relativeOffset` (the `rawSlice`-adjacent primitive, block-\n  relative offset conversion in one place); `collectLinkCodes` now takes `(containerNode,\n  markdown)` and returns `LinkOccurrence[]` (`{code, position}`) instead of `string[]`; the heading\n  case no longer calls it on the heading's own title line, only on a consumed leading paragraph.\n  `ParsedBlockNode.linkCodes` retyped accordingly, threading through `PendingLinkCodes`\n  (`artifacts.ts`) and `extractLinkCodes` unchanged otherwise (it only ever moved the field around,\n  never inspected its shape).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR01V",
    "text": "`apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`'s `resolveBlockLinks`: resolves every code, groups successes by target\n  in a per-block `Map<target, position[]>`, then calls `addWikilink` once per distinct target.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR01W",
    "text": "`props.ts`: `getProps(node, key): string[]` alongside the existing singular `getProp`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR01X",
    "text": "`verify.ts` (§5d): confirms two occurrences of the same target in one block produce one `Link`\n  carrying two `position` props (not two `Link`s), and that each position lands on the opening `[`\n  of its wikilink construct in `block.text`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Y:props:StringProp:00CBFDYY38000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Y:props:StringProp:00CBFDYY3G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR01Y",
    "text": "**Two real bugs surfaced during implementation, both found by the existing test suite catching\nsomething it wasn't specifically written to catch — fixed as part of this step, not deferred:**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Z",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR020"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR01Z",
    "text": "**`vocab.ts`'s `nodeKindFromId` misclassified a `Link`'s own `props` entries.** `SUBDOC_RE`\n  (`/\\/(?:props|links)\\/([A-Za-z]+)\\//`) was matched non-globally, returning the *first* `/props/`\n  or `/links/` segment in an id. Every id shaped this way used to have exactly one such segment —\n  `Link.props` is the first case of a subdocument nested *inside* another subdocument\n  (`.../links/Link/<snowflake>/props/StringProp/<snowflake>`), so the first-match regex found the\n  outer `/links/Link/` and `wrap()`ed every `position` prop as a second `Link` instead of a\n  `StringProp` — quads written correctly, `.key`/`.value` reading back `undefined` on the\n  misclassified wrapper. Fixed: match globally, take the *last* (deepest/rightmost) segment, which\n  is always the id's real, immediate kind regardless of nesting depth.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR020",
    "text": "**Reassigning an embed field only ever detached the old subdocument, never deleted it** —\n  `writeField`'s `clearField` removes the forward reference quad but left whatever it used to point\n  at sitting in the store forever, unreferenced. Harmless to the JSON-LD mirror (`dehydrateToJsonLd`\n  only walks structure reachable from a live top-level sweep, so an orphan is simply never visited,\n  never written) but a real, slowly-growing footprint in the long-lived `service.ts` process, which\n  keeps one `Store` alive across every `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` call for its whole uptime rather than\n  starting fresh each command. Pre-existing since the wikilink-regeneration fix (a dropped stale\n  wikilink `Link` was already leaking its `target`/`predicate` quads), `Link.props` just made each\n  leaked instance bigger (a `props` entry's own `key`/`value` quads too) and this step's own new\n  4-ingestion test in `verify.ts` finally pushed the leak past the dehydrate/rehydrate round-trip's\n  exact-quad-count check. Fixed generally, not narrowly for wikilinks: `writeField` now, for any\n  `storageKind: 'embed'` field, computes which currently-referenced ids survive into the new value\n  and recursively deletes (`deleteSubdocument`, new) whichever don't, before clearing the forward\n  reference — covers every embed field's reassignment (also, incidentally, an equivalent pre-\n  existing leak on an ordinary `props` value change via `carryForwardFields`'s per-key merge in\n  `reconcile.ts`, not just `links`), not just the one call site that surfaced it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR021",
    "text": "**Verified**: `npm run build` (`tsc -b && vite build`) clean; `npm run verify`'s full suite passing,\nincluding both new cases above and (unchanged) every prior one — the dehydrate/rehydrate round-trip\nin particular now passes with the orphan-cleanup fix in place, confirmed via a deliberate before/\nafter check (reverting the fix reproduces the exact quad-count mismatch the fix resolves).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR01E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
