    "title": "00CBFDYXMR027",
    "text": "**Wikilink `Link` identity stability** ([§5](<[[/Aperas-apeironngn-design.md/# ApeironNgn: Embedded Substrate Design/5. Open questions]]>)'s \"tractable half\"). A wikilink `Link` used to get a\nfresh id on every re-ingestion even when its target and occurrence positions hadn't changed at all\n— `hydrateFromParsed` dropped every carried-forward wikilink `Link` unconditionally before\n`resolveBlockLinks` ran, so there was never anything left to reuse. Fixed by moving the decision\ninto `resolveBlockLinks`, where the fresh target/position groupings are actually known:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR022",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR028",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR029",
