  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR02F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR02F",
    "text": "**Tombstones are now visible.** A `(tombstoned)` tag is appended to a node's rendered title line\n  wherever one gets printed: `renderTreeLines` (plain tree), `renderViewLines` (view-based tree), and\n  all three of `renderLinkLine`'s output lines (a link's plain preview, its canonical full render, and\n  its \"see elsewhere\" pointer) — the last of these specifically because a `Link.target` is exactly the\n  \"reached through a still-live reference elsewhere\" case the original trace flagged as the more\n  misleading of the two failure modes (silently showing stale content as current). One shared\n  `tombstoneTag(node)` helper (`node.ts`) keeps the check and the marker text in one place rather than\n  four independent copies.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR02E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
