    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR039",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR039",
    "text": "`kg:path`/`kg:resolve` **do** change, both input and output: `kg:path` (`kgPath.ts`) prints\n  `aperas://tree/<path>` instead of the bare path; `kg:resolve` (`kgResolve.ts`) prints\n  `aperas://id/<id>` instead of the bare id per resolved line (both the plain and `--create-holder`\n  trace output); both also accept the full scheme-qualified forms as input\n  (`resolve.ts`/`resolveCreate.ts`/`tree.ts`'s `resolveTreeRef`), in addition to today's shorthand.",
