    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR03A",
    "text": "`Profile`/`TreeView` get an `aperas://id/...` address like everything else — free, since `nodeIri()`\n  already applies uniformly across every kind.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR036",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR03B",
    "text": "**Verified**: `npm run build` clean; `npm run verify`'s full suite passing (its own scratch-directory\ndemo mints fresh ids under the new scheme, unaffected by the main mirror reset); a live `kg:tree`/\n`kg:path`/`kg:resolve` spot-check against the real (now-empty, freshly re-ingestable) mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR02W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Step 13: `kg:backlinks` — implemented, verified",
    "text": "The missing reverse-lookup counterpart to `kg:unfold`'s forward view of a `Link`: \"what points at\nthis node\" had no CLI answer until now, even though the underlying query was already a one-liner —\n`node.ts`'s generic `backlinks(store, id, field)` helper (used internally for `Profile`→`TreeView`\nlookups) already does exactly this for any reference-kind field, `target` included.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMG00V",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03D",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03E",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03F",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR03D",
    "text": "**Design.** `kg:backlinks -- <path> [--text] [--reload]` resolves `<path>` the usual\n`resolveDeepPath` way, then calls `backlinks(store, id, 'target')` to find every `Link` whose\n`target` is that node. Each `Link`'s owning node — the thing actually doing the referring — comes\nfrom `ownerOfLink` (`node.ts`, previously a private helper inside the view-rendering code, now\nexported for this second caller). One output line per `Link`, not deduped per owner: two separate\nwikilink occurrences in the same block are two distinct backlinks, matching how `kg:link`/\n`kg:unlink` already treat occurrences individually rather than folding them into one owner-level\nentry.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR03E",
    "text": "**Line format**: `<linkId>  [<label>]  <title>` and, with `--text`, an appended `  ║  <abstract>`.\n`<linkId>` is the `Link`'s own id, not a separately-printed owner id — a `Link`'s id already carries\nits owner as a literal prefix (`<ownerId>:links:Link:<snowflake>`), so the one field is\nself-describing rather than needing two. `<label>` is the *owner's* kind (`displayLabel`, the same\n`[heading]`/`[paragraph]`/etc. tag `kg:unfold`'s own child/link previews use) — not a generic\n`[Link]` tag, since the point of a backlink listing is what kind of content is referring in, and\nthat's always knowable (the target is fixed to whatever `<path>` resolved to). `<title>`/`<abstract>`\nare the owner's own `title`/capped preview text, via a small refactor of `kgUnfold.ts`'s existing\n`previewText`: the abstract-only half is now its own exported `nodeAbstract`, with `previewText`\nitself just `title` plus `nodeAbstract` combined — so `kg:backlinks --text` reuses the exact same\nlist/textless-list/truncation rules `kg:unfold`'s previews already apply, rather than a second,\nindependently-maintained copy of them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR03F",
    "text": "New service op `backlinks` (`runBacklinks`, `kgBacklinks.ts`), read-only, `reload`-capable like\n`tree`/`path`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDYXMR03G",
    "text": "**Verified**: `npm run build` clean; `npm run verify`'s full suite passing, plus a new case\nconstructing a live referrer block with a manual link to a fresh target and confirming\n`runBacklinks` returns exactly that one `Link`'s id (correctly prefixed by the referrer's own id),\nthe referrer's real kind/title, no `text` field without `--text`, and a populated one with it; a\nlive `kg:backlinks` spot-check against the real mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDYXMR03H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 5. Open questions",
