    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 1. Motivation",
    "text": "The missing piece for working directly on Apeiron instead of always going through a real markdown\nartifact: a full CRUD surface over nodes, built by reusing the ingestion/reconciliation/parsing\nmachinery that already exists rather than growing a parallel set of write ops. Direct creation and\npositioning target a deep path instead of an artifact path and (mostly) have no file on disk backing\nthem; direct text/children updates are literally the same markdown-ingest pipeline `ArtifactNode`\nalready runs, just retargeted at an arbitrary node instead of a whole document.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ028003",
    "text": "The `holder` flag (`shape.ts`'s `TREE_NODE_SHAPE`, set today only by `--create-holder`'s deep-path\nscaffolding, `resolveCreate.ts`) already does almost exactly the bookkeeping direct creation needs.\nThis doc settles what it actually means, closes the gaps found while working that out, and designs\nthe rest of the CRUD surface around it: positioned insertion/creation/promotion (`kg:insert`),\nabstract placeholder minting (`kg:resolve --create-holder`), content replacement\n(`kg:update`), and recursive removal (`kg:remove`) — alongside the already-implemented `kg:title`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 2. Command map",
