  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800R",
    "text": "The legacy flat `DocumentNode` / `BlockNode` / `SpanNode` schema was entirely eliminated.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800S",
    "text": "Designed and implemented a universal, recursive `BlockNode` topology (Fractal Ontology) rooted in `ArtifactNode`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800T",
    "text": "Schema updated to pure JSON-LD (`schema.json`), avoiding TypeScript interface duplication.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800V",
    "text": "IDs & content fingerprint — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1). `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style identifier (timestamp + machine identity w/ personal failover + sequence counter, 13-char Crockford Base32); `astParser.ts` uses it for every `blockId` instead of the old content hash. `ArtifactNode.contentHash` renamed to `fileHash` throughout (`artifacts.ts`, `schema.json`) to match §1.B's file-domain-only fingerprint — no structural/recursive hash. Verified live: cleared stale pre-redesign `ArtifactNode`/`BlockNode` docs, ran `kg:track`+`kg:ingest` across all 8 artifacts (1144 blocks total, including a 648-block single-artifact burst), zero id collisions. Also found and fixed a real pre-existing bug while verifying: `getArtifactRecord` treated a missing document's raw 404 response (a string, not a thrown error) as a valid record, so untracked artifacts silently reported \"unchanged\" instead of erroring. Reconciliation (best-effort content matching, §1.C history in Appendix F) remains unimplemented — no code needed it yet, since ingestion so far has only ever run against uningested artifacts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800W",
    "text": "Ingestion (`astParser.ts` and `artifacts.ts`) now parses Markdown into a deeply nested tree structure and commits the entire fractal tree via `ArtifactNode.root` in a single TerminusDB operation. Note: a plain `getDocument` read only ever returns `root`/`children` as reference ids, not the nested tree, so full-tree reads go through `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (`graphql.ts`) instead — deliberately, not because the Document API is incapable of it (see `Aperas-architecture.md` §2's \"Read-path note\" for the full investigation, including a filed upstream bug, [terminusdb/terminusdb#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800X",
    "text": "`FolderNode` — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A). `web/src/lib/folders.ts` walks `AperasKG/artifacts/`, builds one `FolderNode` per directory, absorbs each directory's own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`), and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. Wired into `npm run kg:ingest`, which now rebuilds the whole folder tree in the same run as artifact ingestion. Added one concrete `Assertion` class (inherits the previously-uninstantiable abstract `BaseEdge`) to `schema.json`, needed to let `crud.ts`/`woql.ts` actually write/query extrinsic edges — documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.D. `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` are now Snowflake-keyed (`folderId`/`artifactId`), `path` a plain mutable field — see the \"Reconciliation matching\" entry below for the full migration.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800Y",
    "text": "`crud.ts`/`woql.ts`/`graphql.ts`/`verifyPhase0.ts` — **migrated off the dead pre-redesign schema and live-verified**. `crud.ts` now provides `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the new `Assertion` type; `woql.ts` queries `Assertion.source`/`predicate`/`target` (node-typed, not the old flat `xsd:string` `subjectId`/`objectId`) in both directions plus one-hop impact propagation; `graphql.ts` replaced the removed `docId`-scoped block query with `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (bounded-depth nested `root`/`children` selection — GraphQL has no native recursion, so depth is generated explicitly, default 10). `verifyPhase0.ts` was rewritten into a full idempotent, self-cleaning live test of the whole pipeline (AST parsing → track/ingest → GraphQL tree read → `FolderNode` ingestion → `Assertion` CRUD + WOQL traversal → temporal commit management); `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both confirmed passing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13800Z",
    "text": "**Discovered while wiring this up**: TerminusDB enforces referential integrity on document delete — deleting a still-referenced document (e.g. an `ArtifactNode` still listed in a `FolderNode.children`, or a `BlockNode` still pointed to by `ArtifactNode.root`) fails with a `SchemaCheckFailure`, not silently. The best-effort delete helpers in `crud.ts` (`deleteDocumentIfExists`/`deleteDocumentsIfExist`) used to swallow *all* errors on the assumption only \"not found\" could occur — that assumption was wrong and masked this failure mode; they now log instead of swallowing silently, and any caller managing referenced state (like `verifyPhase0.ts`'s cleanup) has to delete in reverse-reference order.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138010",
    "text": "**Heading levels now define tree structure** — **implemented and live-verified**. `astParser.ts` gained `groupByHeadings`, a one-pass depth-stack transform run on every flat mdast sibling list before conversion: each heading becomes the parent of everything until a heading of depth <= its own. A doc with `# Title` / `## Section A` / `## Section B` now parses as nested (`Title` containing `Section A`, `Section B`, each with their own body), not a flat list under the root. Alongside this: every `BlockNode` now carries its raw mdast `type` (needed by reconciliation's leaf/container split below), and `list`/`listItem`/`blockquote` no longer carry the full-subtree-duplicate `text` they used to (confirmed live pre-fix: a `listItem`'s `text` byte-for-byte duplicated its own paragraph child's) — containers now carry no content of their own, by design.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138011",
    "text": "**Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B/§4.A/§4.B/Appendix G). New `web/src/lib/reconcile.ts`: a Gestalt (Ratcliff/Obershelp) tree diff — the longest-common-run algorithm behind Python's `difflib` — applied two-stage per level (Stage A anchors on leaf content by `heading XOR text`; Stage B aligns containers by type within the segments Stage A's anchors define), with ambiguous same-content duplicates declined rather than guessed. Matched `BlockNode`s reuse their old `blockId`; unmatched old ones get an explicit `tombstonedAt` (new field on `BaseNode`, inherited everywhere) rather than being silently orphaned; a block relocated to a different section is detected as a cross-parent move via the same mechanism, one level up from per-parent matching. `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` moved off `Lexical`-on-`path` to Snowflake ids (`artifactId`/`folderId`, same scheme as `BlockNode.blockId`), `path` now a plain mutable field with `title`/`text` added to `ArtifactNode` (filename / naive first-paragraph abstract, matching `FolderNode`'s existing shape) — this is what makes a file/folder rename a field update instead of a delete-and-recreate. Rename detection reuses the identical Gestalt-matching primitive one level up: on every `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` sweep, disk-only and DB-only leftover paths are matched by abstract-text similarity (`matchLeftoverByAbstract`) before falling back to plain add/remove. Wired into `ingestArtifact` (fires whenever a prior ingestion exists), `trackAllArtifacts`, and `ingestFolderTree`; `kgCli.ts` reports renamed/removed/reconciled counts alongside the existing tracked/ingested counts. Live-verified via `verifyPhase0.ts` (edit-and-reingest keeps unrelated `blockId`s stable, reports sane unchanged/added counts) and a manual rename test against a throwaway artifact (`artifactId` and `blockId`s survived a real on-disk move). Migrating the key scheme required clearing all pre-existing `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`/`BlockNode` documents first, since TerminusDB rejects a schema whose new required fields the old instance data doesn't have — the whole KG was then rebuilt from `AperasKG/artifacts/` via a full `kg:track` + `kg:ingest` sweep, per the project's disk-is-source-of-truth model.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138012",
    "text": "**Artifact Projection** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 1 of 3). New `web/src/lib/project.ts` serializes an `ArtifactNode`'s ingested `BlockNode` tree back into Markdown — canonical regeneration, not byte-exact: headings/paragraphs/code round-trip via their raw `title`/`text`, while `list`/`blockquote` are regenerated as clean Markdown (list items always blank-line-separated regardless of original tight/loose style; blockquote `> ` re-prefixed uniformly rather than trusting what the raw text happens to carry). Needed two new captured fields on `BlockNode` — `ordered`/`start` (list numbering) and `checked` (task-list checkbox) — both `Optional`, so unlike the `artifactId`/`type` migration this needed no DB wipe. Exposed via `npm run kg:project -- <path>`. Verified two ways: `verifyPhase0.ts`'s synthetic sample (every branch: ordered/unordered/task lists, nested list, blockquote, code) round-trips with zero drift by reusing `reconcile.ts`'s own matcher as the equivalence check; and, more usefully, running the same check against all 11 real artifacts in `AperasKG/artifacts/` surfaced two genuine bugs no synthetic sample had exercised — a nested code fence's closing `` ``` `` desyncing from its opening one because only a multi-line leaf's *first* line has container-required indentation stripped (every later line keeps its literal original-file column; fixed with a `dedent` normalization), and an *indented* (4-space) code block silently degrading into an ordinary paragraph because its raw slice carries no fence to re-emit (fixed by re-fencing it). After those two fixes, 9 of 11 real artifacts round-trip with zero drift; the other 2 each show one accepted, disclosed difference (absolute code-indentation depth normalized to the minimum; indented-style converted to fenced-style) — real content changes under exact-key matching, not bugs, per the design doc §8.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138013",
    "text": "**Basic Assertion Authoring** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`). New `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI commands (`kgCli.ts`) let a human or agent actually write and inspect a real `Assertion` — previously the only thing that ever called `insertAssertion` was a hardcoded synthetic edge in `verifyPhase0.ts`'s test harness. `source`/`target` accept either a full node id (direct addressing) or a bare artifact/folder path (query-based addressing, resolved via `getArtifactRecord`/the new `getFolderRecord`, artifact tried first since the two never collide) — block-level assertions stay direct-id-only; closing that gap became its own effort, see \"Agentic Query Tools\" below. New narrow `deleteAssertion` (`crud.ts`) does exact source/predicate/target deletion, distinct from the existing blunt `deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` (kept for demo/reset cleanup only). Live end-to-end test against two real artifacts (assert → list → unassert → list-empty) surfaced one real bug: WOQL binds a literal-typed field (`predicate`, `xsd:string`) as a wrapped `{\"@type\", \"@value\"}` object rather than a plain string, unlike node-typed `source`/`target` bindings — `kg:assertions` printed `[object Object]` until fixed with an `unwrapLiteral` helper in `woql.ts`'s `queryNodeAssertions`. Never caught by `verifyPhase0.ts`'s existing Assertion test because that only checks binding presence/membership, never a literal field's actual value. Reordered from Phase 2 into Phase 0 itself (not merely Phase 1) per `Aperas-design.md`'s roadmap, so Phase 1 skill-building starts with it already available.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138014:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ15R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138014:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ15R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ138014",
    "text": "**Agentic Query Tools** — reordered from Phase 1 into Phase 0, design settled (`Aperas-agentic-query-tools-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**. Three CLI tools closing the block-level addressing gap Basic Assertion Authoring (above) left open, and making mode 3 of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A concrete for the first time: `kg:tree` (a deep structural map — depth-first with an optional depth bound; title-only by default), `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` (the actual breadth-first primitive: one level, full content, the first code to ever give the long-inert `unfolded` flag a real effect), and `kg:search` (keyword/regex content search via `WOQL.re` — two unrestricted `title`/`text` queries rather than one per class, since the property names are shared across all three node classes and the id prefix alone already reveals kind). Smoke-tested against the real KG (`kg:tree`, `kg:search`, an `unfold`/`fold` round-trip on a real `BlockNode`, `kg:project`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138015",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138016"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138015",
    "text": "**`unfolded` promoted from `BlockNode` to `BaseNode`** (§4.1) — the field had only ever lived on `BlockNode`, a leftover from before `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` existed as separate concrete classes rather than a deliberate restriction. `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` now persist real state against any node kind, not just display normally with nothing to save for the other two. `kg:tree --unfolded` renders the *combined* shape a sequence of `kg:fold`/`kg:unfold` calls leaves behind in one walk instead of separate scrollback: a node prints full `text` instead of `title` exactly when its own parent has `unfolded === true`, recursion stops at a folded node (with a `(folded — kg:unfold <id> to expand)` hint naming the exact fix), and the walk's own root always stays title-only — composes with `--depth`/`--no-holders` unchanged.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138016",
    "text": "**Real bug found live during this promotion**: `trackArtifact`'s (`artifacts.ts`) and `buildFolderTree`'s (`folders.ts`) record-rebuild paths already carry forward fields like `text`/`root`/`ingestedHash` from the previous document on every re-track/re-ingest, but neither had ever needed to carry forward a *view-state* field before — `unfolded` would have been silently reset to folded on the very next `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` of an `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`, the same class of regression `reconcile.ts` was already fixed for on `BlockNode`. Fixed by adding `unfolded` to `normalizeArtifactDoc`'s carried-forward field set and threading `existingByPath` into `buildFolderTree` (which, unlike `ArtifactNode`, rebuilds its whole tree fresh from disk every run rather than reusing a stored record, so it has nothing to carry forward from without an explicit lookup). Confirmed live: unfolded an `ArtifactNode`, forced a real re-track (content hash change), and it stayed unfolded; same for a `FolderNode` across a direct `ingestFolderTree` re-run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138017",
    "text": "**TreeView & Profile — per-view fold state, links folded into the tree walk** (`Aperas-treeview-design.md`) — **implemented, live-verified against a synthetic graph, not yet run against the real corpus**. Supersedes the `unfolded`-on-`BaseNode` promotion two bullets above entirely: `unfolded` is gone from `BASE_NODE_SHAPE` and every place it touched (`shape.ts`, `reconcile.ts`, `astParser.ts`, `folders.ts`, `apeironNgn/folders.ts`, `apeironNgn/resolveCreate.ts`) — fold state moved off a single flag every viewer shared and onto two new top-level classes: `Profile` (a bucket separating human/agent usage, no auth) and `TreeView` (`unfolds: Set<TreeNode | Link>`, one lens per viewer). `kg:tree`'s `--unfolded` is now `--view <ref>`; `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` target a `TreeView` (`--view`, defaulting to an auto-created `TreeView` named `\"default\"` via `ensureDefaultView`) and touch *exactly* the one specified ref (a `TreeNode` or a bare-id `Link`) — `kg:unfold` never cascades, matching the old `setUnfolded`'s single-flag semantics exactly; `kg:fold` does cascade, removing the ref's own entry plus anything reached from it (structural children, then its own links) that's also separately unfolded, leaving an unrelated `Link` elsewhere that happens to also reach into it untouched. `Link`s are walked alongside structural `children` for the first time, which needed genuinely new logic for a node reachable two ways: its structural home always wins as canonical when it qualifies (in `unfolds` and reachable), any `Link` also reaching it collapses to a short pointer (`(see <path>)`, `TreeNode.toPath()`) instead of re-rendering the subtree, and the canonical position gets tagged `[*]` — recomputed fresh every render from the current `unfolds` set, never cached. `service.ts` gained a second, independent flush interval/dirty-flag pair (`stateDirty`/`STATE_FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS`) writing `Profile`/`TreeView` to a new `AperasKG/Apeiron/.state/`, gitignored in the AperasKG repo's own `.gitignore` — per-viewer UI state, unlike `ArtifactNode`/`BlockNode`/`FolderNode`, isn't authored content `pre-commit` should ever stage. Verified via a synthetic in-memory graph exercising the exact canonical/pointer/cascade scenarios the design doc works through by hand, plus a `.state/` dehydrate→rehydrate round-trip and `ensureDefaultView`'s idempotent bootstrap (same view id reused across repeated calls, not re-minted) — real-corpus exercise against `AperasKG/Apeiron/` is still open.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138018",
    "text": "**Markdown → Fractal Tree Mapping** (`Aperas-markdown-fractal-mapping-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**: `heading`/`listItem` now *consume* (not copy) their leading paragraph as `text`, shallow, one node fewer per section; a `list` now dissolves into whichever `paragraph`/`listItem`/`heading` immediately precedes it (`orderedList`/`startIndex` becoming that adopting node's own `props`) rather than remaining a standalone node, orphaned only when nothing valid precedes it — including the case, found while implementing this, where two lists sit directly adjacent to each other (the second is orphaned, since a `list` itself is never a valid adoption anchor); a new generic `Prop`/`StringProp` mechanism (`BaseNode.props: Set<Prop>`, `props.ts`'s shared `getProp`/`setProp`) replaces the one-field-per-feature pattern, `orderedList`/`startIndex`/`checked` all migrated onto it; YAML frontmatter is extracted via `remark-frontmatter` and stored as one `props` entry on both `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` (`parseMarkdownTree` now returns `{root, frontmatter?}`); `folders.ts`'s README absorption got the same copy-to-consume fix. `project.ts`'s serializer was generalized to match: `heading`/`listItem` emit their consumed `text` before their children, and `renderChildren` scans for contiguous `listItem` runs anywhere in a node's children (not just a dedicated `list` case) using that node's own `props` for numbering. One real GraphQL wrinkle surfaced and fixed: `props: Set<Prop>` can't be queried with an inline fragment on `StringProp` (TerminusDB's generated GraphQL schema makes `Prop` its own concrete type, not an interface `StringProp` implements) — worked around via the generic `_json` field every generated type carries, parsed back into `{key, value}` by `graphql.ts`'s `normalizeProps`. `verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both clean. Same known limitation as Artifact Projection/Agentic Query Tools above: already-ingested real artifacts won't reflect any of this until something forces their re-ingestion.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ138019",
    "text": "**Interactive Title & Cross-Link Authoring** (`Aperas-interactive-summarization-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**. Resolves Stage 2 item 5 below (`Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md`, \"AI-driven summarization... splitting blocks into `title` vs `text`\") — reframed per the project's own zero-background-API principle (`Aperas-design.md` Phase 3 rationale): no LLM call, the CLI just asks whoever is running it (human or an already-in-the-loop coding agent) directly. New `kg:title`/`kg:link` (`kgCli.ts`) prompt interactively for a real title on any still-unlabeled `BlockNode`, or cross-links a block's prose makes that wikilink-syntax extraction (`astParser.ts:92-106`) doesn't catch; both share a new `updateBlockNode` fetch-merge-replace primitive (`crud.ts`) since none existed before. A real regression this design surfaced and fixed before it could ship: `reconcileNode` (`reconcile.ts`) only carried `blockId` forward for a matched (content-unchanged) pair, so a title/link set today would've silently reverted on the artifact's next re-ingest — now carries `title`/`unfolded`/`links` forward too (`carryForwardFields`), and `resolveBlockLinks` (`artifacts.ts`) merges freshly-resolved wikilinks onto that carried-forward `links` instead of overwriting it. Two more bugs found live during this work, both fixed: `graphql.ts`'s block field selection never included `links` at all (so the carry-forward had nothing to carry — added a `links { _id }` selection plus a `normalizeLinks` step converting GraphQL's full-IRI `_id` to the short ref-id form `updateDocument` expects, mirroring the existing `_json`/`normalizeProps` pattern); and `rl.question()` (readline/promises) races against stream-end once real `await`s happen between prompts, which piped/non-interactive stdin (a coding agent driving the tool with pre-computed answers) hits — fixed by consuming the readline interface's own async iterator (`createLineReader`) instead. Live-verified end-to-end: a title and a cross-link set via these commands both survived a real re-ingestion round-trip, confirmed via direct `doc get`, not just the tools' own reported output.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13801A",
    "text": "**Deep Path Resolution** (`Aperas-deep-path-resolution-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**, both directions. `kg:path <id>` (id→path): a new `parent: Optional<BaseNode>` field on `BlockNode` (`astParser.ts`'s `stampParents`, re-run post-reconciliation since `carryForwardFields` reassigns `blockId`s), walked upward by `nodeRef.ts`'s `resolveIdToPath` to the owning `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`. `kg:resolve <path>` (path→id, the reverse): extends `nodeRef.ts`'s `resolveNodeRefOrNull` with the full deep-path grammar — `.`/`..`/leading `/` (Linux-flavored relative addressing, `--base <path>` for batch resolution), exact-then-prefix title matching with \"decline rather than guess\" on ambiguity, and `--create-holder` (a tombstone-like placeholder for a target that doesn't exist yet, tail-aligned `--titles` so a caller only supplies titles for segments actually being created) reaching all the way from a single heading up through imagining whole new `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` chains from nothing. Wired into `artifacts.ts`'s wikilink extractor (forward references to not-yet-written headings now resolve to a holder instead of being silently dropped) and backported into `kg:tree`/`kg:search` (a `(holder)` mark, `--no-holders` to filter — transparent for indentation in `kg:tree`, not a subtree prune, since a holder is per-node not per-branch). New `holder: Optional<xsd:boolean>` field on `BaseNode` (not a `Prop` — a first-class concept needed on every node kind, not parser-derived per-node metadata); `ArtifactNode.fileHash`/`lastTrackedAt` made `Optional` to let a holder `ArtifactNode` exist with no real file behind it yet.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13801B",
    "text": "Several real bugs found live during implementation, none of them the original design's own text (all consistent with what `Aperas-deep-path-resolution-design.md` itself now documents inline, §4/§7): a heading's leading `#`/`##` slugifying to leading dashes made prefix matching dead on arrival until the candidate's dashes were stripped before the `startsWith` check; writing a holder directly under an `ArtifactNode` failed schema check because its one child is the singular `root` field, not a `children` List; and, most fundamentally, resolving wikilinks *before* the tree's own write was a genuine chicken-and-egg bug (the implicit base needs an already-persisted `.parent` chain, so anything brand-new in the current edit would resolve against the *previous* ingestion's stale tree) — fixed by moving link resolution to a separate pass after the write, extracting/stripping each block's raw `linkCodes` beforehand since `schema.json` has no such field and leaving it in fails the write itself. `verifyPhase0.ts`'s wikilink test extended to cover all three shapes end-to-end (a bare snowflake code, a forward reference that becomes a real holder, and a still-genuinely-unresolvable one that correctly declines) rather than just the original single self-link case.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ13801C",
    "text": "**ApeironNgn CRUD surface + the Phase 0 → Phase 1 direction flip** (`Aperas-crud-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified end-to-end against the real service/CLI/mirror**, the closing act of Phase 0. Full command surface for working directly on the graph instead of always going through a real markdown artifact: `kg:insert` (unified move/promote/create for `BlockNode`s, positioned via `--after`/`--before`), `kg:resolve --create-holder` (abstract placeholder minting, internally unified with the rest of deep-path resolution — a partially-real-prefix-then-gap case that used to mint a wrongly-typed node is fixed), `kg:update`/`--text-only` (generalizes `ArtifactNode.ingestFromDisk`'s own parse/reconcile mechanism to any existing node), and `kg:remove` (recursive soft tombstone, never a hard delete). `holder` (minted by `--create-holder`) settled as a flag, not a kind — reconciliation-survival metadata, not a separate type — with every write path that can promote one (disk-match, projection, explicit positioning) now correctly clearing it; a same-target splice-ordering bug and a Folder/Artifact rename-sweep gap (a top-level holder always looked removed to it) were both found and fixed live before this shipped.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG008",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG009",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801G:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5M0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801G:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5M0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ13801G",
    "text": "Not yet started",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00C",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00D",
