    "title": "00CBFDZ1W0029",
    "text": "**Default `Profile`/`TreeView` for a bare CLI call with no `--view`** — implemented as proposed:\n  the literal string `\"default\"`. `node.ts`'s `ensureDefaultView(store)` resolves `TreeView` where\n  `name === \"default\"` via exact-literal lookup (the same pattern `findByExactPath`, `tree.ts`,\n  already uses for `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode.path`), auto-creating it — and a `Profile` with\n  `handle: \"default\"` to own it — on first miss, so a caller never needs to know a generated id or\n  run a one-time setup step. `--view` only ever takes a `TreeView` ref directly (there's no separate\n  `--profile` flag anywhere in this design), so `Profile.handle` resolution only matters for that\n  one bootstrap path, not for everyday CLI use. Used by `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` when `--view` is omitted;\n  `kg:tree` deliberately does *not* fall back to it ([§5](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/5. Rendering: three display tiers; `kg:unfold` touches exactly one ref]]>)) — omitting `--view` there keeps the plain\n  no-view default instead. See [§11](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/11. `Profile` becomes real identity — `kg:profile`]]>) for why this bootstrap doesn't make `\"default\"` permanently\n  special beyond that one first-use moment.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0025",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 11. `Profile` becomes real identity — `kg:profile`",
    "text": "**Status: designed, not yet implemented.**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002C",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002D",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002M",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8003",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8004",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B:links:Link:00CBFDZ2XR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001T",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B:links:Link:00CBFDZ2XR000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ2XR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "19"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B:links:Link:00CBFDZ2XR002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001V",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B:links:Link:00CBFDZ2XR002:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ2Y0000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "317"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B:links:Link:00CBFDZ2Y0001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0008",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002B:links:Link:00CBFDZ2Y0001:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ2Y0002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "599"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002B",
    "text": "`Profile` started ([§7](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/7. `Profile`: lightweight identity, still no auth]]>)) as pure internal bucketing — just enough to keep separate `TreeView`s from\ncolliding. Once it needs to be addressable from a CLI and hand-edited directly in its own mirror\nfile ([§8](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/8. Git separation: a]]>)) like a settings file, \"a label with no key\" stopped being enough: it needs a stable slug\ndistinct from whatever gets displayed, an open category, and somewhere to hang arbitrary\npreferences. [§3](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/3. Data model: `Profile` and `TreeView`]]>)'s schema reflects that:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002C",
    "text": "```\nProfile\n  handle:      One, xsd:string           -- stable, addressable slug (\"default\", \"will\", \"claude-agent-1\")\n  name:        Optional xsd:string       -- display/social name\n  kind:        Optional xsd:string       -- open label, suggested {\"human\",\"agent\"}; left unset if not given\n  preferences: Set, embed -> StringProp  -- arbitrary key/value bag\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002D:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ22G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002D:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ22G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002D",
    "text": "Two deliberate non-additions:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002E",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002E:links:Link:00CBFDZ2YG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0008",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002E:links:Link:00CBFDZ2YG000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ2YG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "157"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002E",
    "text": "**No stored `views` field.** A `Profile`'s owned `TreeView`s (and any future non-`TreeView` view\n  kind — a \"linear view,\" say) are still found the same way [§3](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/3. Data model: `Profile` and `TreeView`]]>) already resolves\n  `Profile > TreeView`: reverse-querying `profile` (`backlinks(store, id, 'profile')`).\n  Kind-agnostic for free — a future view kind needs zero extra plumbing here as long as it also\n  stores a forward `profile` reference.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002F",
    "text": "**`preferences` reuses the existing `props`/`StringProp` embed shape** (`BlockNode.props`) rather\n  than a new subdocument type — same encode/decode/dehydrate machinery, zero new plumbing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G:links:Link:00CBFDZ2Z8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001V",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G:links:Link:00CBFDZ2Z8000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ2Z8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "140"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G:links:Link:00CBFDZ2Z8002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001T",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G:links:Link:00CBFDZ2Z8002:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ2Z8003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "287"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ22R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ22R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002G",
    "text": "**`kg:profile` — deliberately minimal**, since most of a `Profile`'s content is meant to be viewed\nand edited directly in `Profile.jsonld` ([§8](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/8. Git separation: a]]>)) — the same posture as any other settings file,\nmatching [§7](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/7. `Profile`: lightweight identity, still no auth]]>)'s \"no auth, no enforced enum\" stance:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002H",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002J",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002K"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002H",
    "text": "`kg:profile create <handle> [--name <name>] [--kind <kind>]` — `kind` (like `name`) is `Optional`,\n  left unset if omitted rather than defaulted to a sentinel value.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002J",
    "text": "`kg:profile list [<handle>]` — no arg: one line per `Profile` (`handle`/`name`/`kind`/owned-view\n  count); given a `handle`: full detail, adding `preferences` and the owned views' own ids/names.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002K",
    "text": "`kg:profile remove <handle>` — cascade-deletes every `TreeView` it owns first (the same\n  recursive-delete posture `hardDeleteNode` already takes for embedded subdocuments and tombstoned\n  subtrees elsewhere in the model — a `Profile` gone with its `TreeView`s left dangling would be a\n  worse state than either \"keep both\" or \"remove both\").",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002M",
    "text": "No rename or per-preference-key subcommand — a direct edit to `Profile.jsonld` already covers both,\nand adding CLI surface for something already reachable by hand-editing the mirror would just be two\nways to do the same thing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N:links:Link:00CBFDZ2ZR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0024",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N:links:Link:00CBFDZ2ZR000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ2ZR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "566"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ230000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ230001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W002N",
    "text": "**View lifecycle — `kg:profile *-view`.** A `TreeView`'s own `name` plays exactly the addressable\nrole `Profile.handle` does: a stable, human-chosen slug, not a raw node id — so `TREE_VIEW_SHAPE`\ntightens `name` from `Optional` to `One` to match, and it gets the same \"set up before use\"\ndiscipline. `--view <name>` (`kg:tree`/`kg:unfold`/`kg:fold`) already refuses an unrecognized name\noutright rather than silently minting one on first typo (`resolveTreeView`'s existing behavior,\nunchanged) — the one exception stays `\"default\"`, still auto-created on first use ([§10](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/10. Open questions — all resolved]]>)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8000",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8001",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8000",
    "text": "`kg:profile create-view <name> --profile <handle>` — mints a new, empty `TreeView` owned by the\n  named `Profile` (which must already exist — no implicit profile creation here either). Rejects a\n  duplicate `name`, the same uniqueness check `kg:profile create` already applies to `handle`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8001",
    "text": "`kg:profile list-view [<name>]` — no arg: one line per `TreeView` (`name`/owning `Profile`\n  `handle`/unfold count); given a `name`: full detail (its `unfolds` set).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8002",
    "text": "`kg:profile remove-view <name>` — deletes exactly that one `TreeView`, without touching its owning\n  `Profile` — the single-view counterpart to `kg:profile remove <handle>`'s all-at-once cascade.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8003",
    "text": "Global uniqueness, not per-profile: two different `Profile`s can never have same-named views,\nmatching `Profile.handle`'s own single flat namespace rather than adding a second, profile-scoped\none.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8004:links:Link:00CBFDZ308000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0024",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8004:links:Link:00CBFDZ308000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ308001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "44"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8004",
    "text": "**Auto-init is not the same as hardcoded.** [§10](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/10. Open questions — all resolved]]>)'s `\"default\"` `Profile`/`TreeView` bootstrap\n(`ensureDefaultView`) is the *only* place either one gets special-cased — a one-time\ncreate-if-missing convenience so a fresh install works with no setup step, now creating a `Profile`\nwith `handle: \"default\"` rather than just a bare `name` (`kind` stays unset, same as any other\nfreshly-created `Profile` with no `--kind` given). Once that bootstrap has run once, `\"default\"` is\nan ordinary row: listed by `kg:profile list` like any other, hand-editable\nin the mirror like any other, and removable via `kg:profile remove default` (cascading to its\nviews) exactly like any other `handle` — nothing downstream of that one bootstrap moment ever\ntreats it as forever-privileged.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8005:links:Link:00CBFDZ30G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001V",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8005:links:Link:00CBFDZ30G000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ30G001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "37"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8005",
    "text": "**Git/mirror placement**: covered in [§8](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/8. Git separation: a]]>) — `Profile` is dehydrated to the tracked content mirror\n(`DEHYDRATE_CLASSES`), not `.state/`; whether it's actually committed in a given repo is that\nrepo's own `.gitignore` decision, not something this design enforces.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W002A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 12. Depth legibility in plain-text tree output",
    "text": "**Status: implemented.**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8007",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8008",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8009",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800A",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800B",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800C",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8007:links:Link:00CBFDZ310000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W000C",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8007:links:Link:00CBFDZ310000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ310001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "201"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8007",
    "text": "`renderTreeLines`/`renderViewLines` (`node.ts`) indent each depth level with two literal spaces\n(`'  '.repeat(depth)`) and nothing else — the only design examples with box-drawing characters\n(├─/│/└─, [§4](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/4. Worked example]]>)'s worked-example trees) are illustrative, not what the CLI actually emits.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8008",
    "text": "**The problem**: recovering a line's depth from plain-space indentation requires already knowing\nthe per-level width (2, today) and dividing the leading-space count by it — that convention isn't\nvisible in the output itself, for a human or an agent reader alike. Worse, the signal is fragile:\nrepeated spaces are exactly the kind of thing some renderers, terminals, or copy/paste paths\nnormalize or collapse, which would silently corrupt the only place depth is encoded.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8009:links:Link:00CBFDZ31G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W000C",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8009:links:Link:00CBFDZ31G000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ31G001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "70"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8009",
    "text": "**Option A — full box-drawing tree art**, connecting siblings the way [§4](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/4. Worked example]]>)'s illustrative examples\ndo: visually the most familiar (matches `tree`/`ls -R`-style output), but it doesn't actually fix\nthe problem above — depth is still `prefixWidth / perLevelWidth`, just spread across a 2-3-glyph\nwide unit instead of a 2-space one, so a reader still needs the same outside knowledge of that\nwidth. It also carries a real implementation cost: which corner glyph a line gets (├─ vs └─)\ndepends on whether it's the last sibling, and whether an ancestor's continuation column renders │\nor blank depends on whether *that* ancestor was itself a last sibling — producing this needs a\nfull pass with sibling lookahead first, not the current single top-down recursive emit\n(`renderTreeLines`/`renderViewLines` emit each line as they visit it, in one pass).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800A",
    "text": "**Option B — a single repeated marker per level**, e.g. `'│ '.repeat(depth)` in place of\n`'  '.repeat(depth)`: the marker is non-whitespace, so depth becomes \"count the marker glyph before\nthe first non-marker character\" — self-describing from the output alone, with no per-repo\nindent-width convention to know in advance, and no ambiguity from whitespace-collapsing. To a human\neye it reads as a set of clean vertical guide lines — mechanically close to what box-drawing's own\n│ continuation column already gives — without option A's last-sibling lookahead cost: the existing\nsingle recursive pass is unchanged, only the literal indent string changes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800B",
    "text": "**Decided: option B**, marker `'│ '` (one `│` plus one space, 2 characters per level — the same\nwidth as today's plain 2-space indent, just with the leading space replaced by a visible glyph).\nEvery indent site in `node.ts` switches uniformly: `renderTreeLines`, `renderViewLines`,\n`renderLinkLine`, and the `…`-pruned-children marker (currently all `'  '.repeat(...)` at various\ndepths) all become `'│ '.repeat(...)`. No distinction between a continuing branch and a last\nsibling — every level renders the same marker regardless of position, unlike true box-drawing art,\nwhich needs sibling lookahead to pick between `│` and blank per level (option A's cost, avoided\nhere).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800C:links:Link:00CBFDZ31R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W000C",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800C:links:Link:00CBFDZ31R000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ31R001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "17"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800C",
    "text": "Applying this to [§4](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/4. Worked example]]>)'s post-fold worked example (the tree after `kg:fold 1`/`kg:fold 3`):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800D",
