    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800F",
    "text": "A **viewcone**'s boundary is purely structural: the *entire* structural subtree under an apex node\n— every descendant, regardless of `unfolds` — the \"cone\" shape a containment tree traces out below\nany one of its nodes. This is why it's called a cone, not a \"viewset\": it's a tree shape, defined\nby `parent`-chain containment alone, the same shape [§4](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/4. Worked example]]>)-[§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>) already render, just not yet named or\ngeneralized past `Root`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G:links:Link:00CBFDZ350000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0016",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G:links:Link:00CBFDZ350000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ350001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "85"
          },
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G:links:Link:00CBFDZ350000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ358000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "604"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G:links:Link:00CBFDZ358001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G:links:Link:00CBFDZ358001:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ358002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "225"
          },
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G:links:Link:00CBFDZ358001:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ358003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "1031"
          },
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800G:links:Link:00CBFDZ358001:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ358004",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "1551"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800G",
    "text": "**A single iteration of the 2-pass algorithm is bounded entirely by its viewcone** — [§5](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/5. Rendering: three display tiers; `kg:unfold` touches exactly one ref]]>)/[§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>)'s\nexisting rules apply completely unchanged *inside* one cone: a node's tier (full/preview/\ntitle-only) still comes from whether it and its structural ancestors are in `unfolds`; a link\nlisted only because its owner is genuinely unfolded ([§5](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/5. Rendering: three display tiers; `kg:unfold` touches exactly one ref]]>) rule a) still renders as a flat preview,\nnever recursing, regardless of where its target sits. The one thing that's new: **a link that is\nitself in `unfolds` (rule b) and whose target falls *outside* the current cone** doesn't have a\ncanonical position this pass can resolve on its own ([§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>)'s canonical-home computation only knows\nabout nodes inside the cone it was computed for) — that's the trigger to zoom: recurse the whole\n2-pass algorithm again with the target as the new apex, producing a nested viewcone. A rule-b link\nwhose target falls *inside* the current cone needs no recursion at all — it's projected in the very\nsame second pass, by the very same existing [§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>) rule (pointer to the qualifying home, or full render\nif no home qualifies).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800H",
    "text": "This is not blind recursion — it only ever follows a link that is *actually* in `unfolds`, so it's\nbounded by however deep that set's own link-chain happens to go, never by an arbitrary depth limit.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800J:links:Link:00CBFDZ360000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W000C",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800J:links:Link:00CBFDZ360000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ360001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "314"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800J:links:Link:00CBFDZ360002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800J:links:Link:00CBFDZ360002:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ360003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "401"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800J",
    "text": "**`Root` never escapes its own cone.** `cone(Root)` is the entire graph — every node sits somewhere\nunder `Root` structurally, by construction — so no link, unfolded or not, can ever have a target\noutside it. Zooming to `Root` therefore degenerates to exactly today's flat, already-implemented\nsingle-pass render ([§4](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/4. Worked example]]>)-[§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>)): viewcone zoom is a strict generalization, introducing new behavior only\nfor a non-`Root` apex.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800K",
    "text": "Following the *parent* chain upward for \"broader context\" is a real, common reading pattern\n(checking a document's breadcrumb trail, not just its outbound links) but is navigation\nmethodology layered on top, not part of the projection algorithm above — `parent` is not folded\ninto `links` and needs no change to the 2-pass algorithm itself.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800M",
    "text": "**Prior art: Logseq's block zoom** (Logseq ← Roam Research ← WorkFlowy's \"zoom\" ← outliners'\ngeneric \"hoist,\" at least as far back as Dave Winer's ThinkTank/MORE, 1984). Logseq's \"zoom into a\nblock\" is exactly a single, non-recursive\nviewcone — the clicked block becomes the apex, its structural descendants the whole view, with no\nnotion of following a logical (page-)link outward as part of the same zoomed render. Logseq\napproximates the \"broader logical context\" this design's recursion gives natively by stacking\nseparately-zoomed blocks as independent panes in its right sidebar — each pane its own flat,\nstructural-only zoom, manually opened one at a time, never unified into one render the way a\nviewcone's nested cones are. This design folds both structural and logical (`Link`) escape into the\nsame recursive projection, computed and rendered as a single tree rather than a user-assembled\nstack of separate views.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N:links:Link:00CBFDZ36G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W000C",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N:links:Link:00CBFDZ36G000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ36G001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "8"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### 13.1 Worked example",
    "text": "Reusing [§4](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/4. Worked example]]>)'s exact sample graph and its exact unfold sequence (`unfolds` = `{1, 1.2, 2, 2.2, 3.3.1,\nLink(1.l1→2.2), Link(2.2.l1→1.2)}` — nothing hypothetical added), **zooming to apex `1`**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800P",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Q",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800R",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800S",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800T",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800V",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800W",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800X",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Y",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Z"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800P",
    "text": "```\nRoot\n├─ 1\n│  ├─ 1.1\n│  ├─ 1.2\n│  │  ├─ 1.2.1\n│  │  ├─ 1.2.2\n│  │  ├─ l1 → 2.1\n│  │  └─ l2 → 3.1\n│  ├─ 1.3\n│  ├─ l1 → 2.2\n│  └─ l2 → 3.3\n├─ 2\n│  ├─ 2.1\n│  ├─ 2.2\n│  │  ├─ 2.2.1\n│  │  ├─ 2.2.2\n│  │  └─ l1 → 1.2\n│  ├─ l1 → 1.2\n│  └─ l2 → 3.3\n└─ 3\n   ├─ 3.1\n   ├─ 3.2\n   ├─ 3.3\n   │  ├─ 3.3.1{.1,.2}\n   │  └─ 3.3.2\n   └─ l1 → 1.1\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Q:links:Link:00CBFDZ378000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0016",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Q:links:Link:00CBFDZ378000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ378001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "184"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Q:links:Link:00CBFDZ378002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Q:links:Link:00CBFDZ378002:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ378003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "324"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800Q",
    "text": "**Stage 1 — `zoom(1)` alone.** `cone(1)` = `1`'s entire structural subtree,\n`{1.1, 1.2{1.2.1, 1.2.2}, 1.3}` — every descendant, whether or not it's unfolded. Rendered by the\nunchanged [§5](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/5. Rendering: three display tiers; `kg:unfold` touches exactly one ref]]>)/[§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>) rules:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800R",
    "text": "```\n1{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.1{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.2{title,abstract} [*]\n│  ├─ 1.2.1{title,abstract}\n│  ├─ 1.2.2{title,abstract}\n│  ├─ 1.2.l1→2.1{title,abstract}\n│  └─ 1.2.l2→3.1{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.3{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.l1→2.2  ⇒ escapes cone(1) — pending, resolved by zoom(2.2) below\n└─ 1.l2→3.3{title,abstract}   — rule a only (never itself unfolded): flat preview, never escapes\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800S",
    "text": "`1.2` gets `[*]`, a canonical home fully resolved *within* `cone(1)` — its own links `l1→2.1`/\n`l2→3.1` are rule-a-only, so neither escapes. The only thing left unresolved at this stage is\n`1.l1→2.2`: itself in `unfolds` (rule b), target outside `cone(1)`. **Nothing about `2.2`'s own\ncontent — including its link `2.2.l1`** — is touched yet at this stage; `2.2` is only known here as\nan escaping link's target, not yet as an apex of its own.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800T",
    "text": "**Stage 2 — `zoom(2.2)`**, triggered by the escape above. `cone(2.2)` = `{2.2.1, 2.2.2}` — `2.2`'s\nown children only; `2` (its structural *parent*, an ancestor not a descendant) is not part of this\ncone at all, regardless of `2` being separately in `unfolds`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800V",
    "text": "```\n2.2{title,abstract}\n├─ 2.2.1{title,abstract}\n├─ 2.2.2{title,abstract}\n└─ 2.2.l1→1.2  ⇒ escapes cone(2.2) — target already canonical in cone(1)\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800W",
    "text": "This is where `2.2.l1` is touched for the first time — not at stage 1, only once `2.2` itself\nbecomes an apex. It escapes again, this time back to `1.2`, which already has a canonical home in\n`cone(1)`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800X",
    "text": "**Combined into one tree** (nesting stage 2 at the point stage 1 escaped):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800Y",
    "text": "```\n1{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.1{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.2{title,abstract} [*]\n│  ├─ 1.2.1{title,abstract}\n│  ├─ 1.2.2{title,abstract}\n│  ├─ 1.2.l1→2.1{title,abstract}\n│  └─ 1.2.l2→3.1{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.3{title,abstract}\n├─ 1.l1→2.2{title,abstract}\n│  ├─ 2.2.1{title,abstract}\n│  ├─ 2.2.2{title,abstract}\n│  └─ 2.2.l1→1.2  [*see 1/1.2]       — cone(1) is a container of cone(2.2); its home wins (§13.2)\n└─ 1.l2→3.3{title,abstract}\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Z:links:Link:00CBFDZ37R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W000C",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800Z:links:Link:00CBFDZ37R000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ37R001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "47"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W800Z",
    "text": "`2` and `3.3.1` — both genuinely in `unfolds` ([§4](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/4. Worked example]]>) steps 5 and 7) — never appear anywhere in either\nstage or the combined tree: neither ever sits inside a cone this chain actually visits, nor is\neither ever an escaping link's target. Their `unfolds` membership is simply never consulted, a\nconcrete demonstration of \"bounded by which links are unfolded and where they point,\" not by\nexhaustively walking every unfolded node in the graph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### 13.2 Resolved: canonical-home is per-cone internally, containment-ordered across cones",
    "text": "Neither of the two flat alternatives originally posed — not one global map computed as if the\nwhole recursion were a single flat pass, and not fully independent per-cone maps with no\ncross-cone awareness at all. Two different rules, depending on whether the two competing\npositions sit in the same cone or not:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8011",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8012",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8013",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8014"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8011:links:Link:00CBFDZ388000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8011:links:Link:00CBFDZ388000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ388001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "40"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8011",
    "text": "**Within one viewcone**, unchanged from [§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>): a node's own structural position, when it qualifies\n(visible, and separately in `unfolds`), is always canonical over any link *inside that same cone*\npointing at it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8010",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8012",
    "text": "**Across viewcones**, canon follows containment: when a link inside a nested (recursively-spawned)\ncone escapes to a node that already has a canonical position in one of that cone's **containers**\n— the cone(s) whose own escaping link led, directly or transitively, to this nested cone existing\nat all — the container's position wins, and the nested link becomes a pointer back to it. In the\nworked example, `cone(2.2)` exists only because `cone(1)`'s own link `1.l1` escaped to it, making\n`cone(1)` a container of `cone(2.2)`. `1.2` is already canonical in `cone(1)`, so `2.2.l1→1.2`\nresolves as a pointer: `2.2.l1→1.2  [*see 1/1.2]` — not a re-expansion.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8010",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8013:links:Link:00CBFDZ38G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0024",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8013:links:Link:00CBFDZ38G000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ38R000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "244"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8013",
    "text": "**Only when two cones share no containment relation at all** (neither a container of the other —\ntwo independent zooms, or two sibling nested cones spawned from unrelated escaping links) is it a\ngenuine, unprincipled tie: resolved the same way [§10](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/10. Open questions — all resolved]]>) already accepts for the flat single-apex case\n— whichever gets projected first, a fact of implementation-internal order, not a structural rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8010",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8014:links:Link:00CBFDZ390000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0024",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8014:links:Link:00CBFDZ390000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ390001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "326"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8014",
    "text": "Termination follows the same shape as before: any link from a nested cone back toward a position\nalready held by one of its own containers stops there rather than re-expanding. The only case left\nunresolved is a tie between cones with no containment relation — already an accepted, unprincipled\ncase elsewhere in this design ([§10](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/10. Open questions — all resolved]]>)), not a new gap this introduces.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8010",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### 13.3 Known gap: upward-pointing links (identified, not yet fixed)",
    "text": "`parent` is itself an implicit upward link — every `BlockNode` already carries one, silently.\nNothing stops a wikilink from making that same edge *explicit*: a block linking to its own\ncontainer, at any distance. Two shapes this takes, the second reducing to the first.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8016",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8017",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801A",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801B",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801E",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8016:links:Link:00CBFDZ39G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8016:links:Link:00CBFDZ39G000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ39G001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "313"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8016",
    "text": "**Case 1 — self-cycle.** A `Link`'s target is a structural ancestor of its own owner block. If that\nancestor still sits *inside* the current cone (between the query's apex and the link's own owner),\nnothing special happens — it's an ordinary in-cone target, resolved like any other by\n`hasStructuralPresence` and [§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>)'s rule. But if the target sits *above* the apex itself —\noutside the current cone entirely — the escaping-link machinery spawns a nested cone for it, and\nsince the target is an ancestor, `cone(target)` *contains* `cone(apex)` wholesale rather than\nsitting beside it, the way a genuinely independent escaping target would.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8017:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ258000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8017:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ25G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8017",
    "text": "**Case 2 — a link to `D`, where `D`'s cone contains an already-active cone `C`.**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8018",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8019"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8018:links:Link:00CBFDZ3A0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8010",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8018:links:Link:00CBFDZ3A0000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ3A0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "233"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8018",
    "text": "**2.1, `C` is itself a nested (non-initial) cone** — already correct today, automatically:\n  `zs.canonical` is one map shared across the whole recursion, and a container cone is always\n  discovered before the nested cones it spawns ([§13.2](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/13. Viewcone Zoom: projecting from an arbitrary apex/13.2 Resolved: canonical-home is per-cone internally, containment-ordered across cones]]>)). Whatever `C`'s apex already resolved to\n  wins; a link to `D` (or to anything already inside `C`) simply becomes a pointer. No fix needed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8017",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8019:links:Link:00CBFDZ3AG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W001H",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8019:links:Link:00CBFDZ3AG000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ3AG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "675"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W8019",
    "text": "**2.2, `C` is the query's own initial/root cone** — this is where it breaks, and it's just case 1\n  restated: the initial cone has no outer container of its own to defer to, so a link escaping to\n  its ancestor `D` doesn't nest *beside* the already-discovered root cone, it nests *around* it.\n  `discoverCone(D)` re-derives `neededChildren`/`unfoldedTreeIds` for everything already inside the\n  root cone, double-counting `attemptCount` for all of it — and if `D` itself later becomes a\n  rendered canonical position (some other link targets it and wins), its recursion walks straight\n  back down through the root cone's own content and reprints it: the same duplication bug [§6](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/6. Two paths to the same node: one canonical, the rest become pointers]]>)\n  just fixed, recurring one level up.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8017",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801A:links:Link:00CBFDZ3B0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W800E",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801A:links:Link:00CBFDZ3B0000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ3B0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "238"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W801A",
    "text": "This entire gap only exists because `kg:tree`'s query apex is routinely *not* the true graph\n`Root` — an `ArtifactNode` deep inside the folder tree, with real ancestors above it. Zooming to the\nactual `Root` sidesteps it by construction ([\"`Root` never escapes its own cone\"](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/13. Viewcone Zoom: projecting from an arbitrary apex]]>), above) — the gap only\nsurfaces once viewcone zoom is used from a non-`Root` apex, which is its entire purpose.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801B:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ25G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801B:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ25R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W801B",
    "text": "**Two ways to close this gap**, weighed against each other:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801C",
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W801C",
    "text": "**Stop recursion at a container of the initial cone.** Before spawning a nested cone for an\n   escaping target, check whether the target is an ancestor of the query's *initial* apex — one\n   upward walk, equivalently `isInCone(rootApexId, targetId)`. If so, decline to recurse into it at\n   all: render the link as a flat, non-recursing reference (rule a's shape, or a distinct tag making\n   clear \"points outside the current view\") instead of a full rule-b expansion.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W801D",
    "text": "**Find the maximal cone first, re-root the whole projection there.** Detect every upward escape\n   reachable from the initial apex — potentially transitively, since an ancestor's own link could\n   point even further up — compute the highest such ancestor, and run the entire 2-pass algorithm\n   from that bigger apex instead of the one actually requested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801E:links:Link:00CBFDZ3B8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W0016",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801E:links:Link:00CBFDZ3B8000:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ3BG000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "481"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W801E",
    "text": "**Chosen: option 1.** Option 2 is structurally \"more correct\" in isolation — it turns every case\ninto an ordinary downward containment relationship, eliminating the inverted container/nested\nmismatch entirely — but it silently changes what the query is even about: `kg:tree\nAperas-apeironngn-design.md` would stop being scoped to that document the moment some deep paragraph\nhappens to link back to its own containing folder, promoting an apex the user never asked for and\npulling [§5](<[[/Aperas-treeview-design.md/# TreeView & Profile — Design/5. Rendering: three display tiers; `kg:unfold` touches exactly one ref]]>)'s Root-child unconditional-preview rule over siblings and unrelated branches under it.\nIt also isn't actually cheaper — finding \"maximal\" needs its own pre-pass walking upward escapes to\na fixed point before the real projection can even start, just a differently-shaped cost than\noption 1's. `kg:tree`'s contract is \"show me the tree from *this* apex, nothing above it\"; option 1\npreserves that contract exactly, degrading an upward-pointing link to a flat reference rather than\npromoting the whole view outward to accommodate it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W801F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ1W801F",
    "text": "**Status: direction chosen (option 1), not yet implemented.** Still needs the exact detection\n(likely generalizing past just the *initial* apex to any cone already active in the current\ndiscovery chain, not only the root) and the exact rendering shape for a link that declines to\nrecurse this way.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ1W8015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ418001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ418001:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ420000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ418001:props:StringProp:00CBFDZ420001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBFDZ418001",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CBFDW95G000",
    "type": "list",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ418002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ418002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBFDZ418002",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ418001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ418003"
    ]
  },
  {
