    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY80017",
    "text": "**`appendOrderedChild` (node.ts:98-105) is append-only** — `siblingIndex` is always assigned\n  `siblingCount`, i.e. current tail. No primitive exists for inserting at an arbitrary position —\n  closed by `insertOrderedChild`, [§7](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/7. `kg:insert` — position, promote, or create]]>).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002G:links:Link:00CBHMH0K8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028013",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002G:links:Link:00CBHMH0K8000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0KG000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "55"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002G",
    "text": "`project.ts`'s renderer excluding tombstoned children ([§6](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/6. Bookkeeping gaps found while designing this (all currently real, all need closing)]]>)) — found during the live\n   end-to-end CLI pass below: `kg:remove` on a real scratch artifact correctly tombstoned a block\n   (confirmed via `kg:tree`), but `kg:project` on the same artifact still rendered that block's\n   content. `renderChildren` now filters `tombstonedAt` children before serializing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ02802E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002H:links:Link:00CBHMH0M0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBHMH0KR000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002H:links:Link:00CBHMH0M0000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0M0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "80"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002H",
    "text": "`kg:ingest`'s confirm/`--force` gate on destructive disk-driven reconciliation ([§14](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/14. `kg:ingest`'s confirm/--force gate on destructive reconciliation]]>)) — found\n    the same live end-to-end pass: `kg:insert`-authored content on an already-real artifact,\n    never yet projected, was silently tombstoned the next time a real disk-driven `kg:ingest` ran\n    against that file for an unrelated reason.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ02802E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002J:links:Link:00CBHMH0MG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Y",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002J:links:Link:00CBHMH0MG000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0MG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "22"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002J",
    "text": "`kg:track --reverse` ([§15](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/15. `kg:track --reverse` — tracking, pointed the other way]]>)) — new `projectedHash` field on `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`, set by\n    `kg:project` on every real write; `runReverseTrack` reports never-projected/changed-since-\n    projection/stale-on-disk drift, read-only, no mutation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ02802E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002K:links:Link:00CBHMH0N0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBHMH0KR000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002K:links:Link:00CBHMH0N0000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0N0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "62"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002K",
    "text": "`kg:track`'s own confirm/`--force` gate on its removal sweep ([§14](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/14. `kg:ingest`'s confirm/--force gate on destructive reconciliation]]>)) — the follow-up flagged\n    as out of scope when §14 first shipped, now closed the same way; `pre-commit`/`post-index-change`\n    updated to pass `--force` so their existing unattended behavior doesn't change.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ02802E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002M:links:Link:00CBHMH0NG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80035",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002M:links:Link:00CBHMH0NG000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0NG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "97"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002M",
    "text": "`kg:project`'s confirm/`--force` gate against clobbering disk changes it doesn't know about\n    ([§16](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/16. `kg:project`'s own reciprocal gap — it could silently clobber a hand-edited file]]>)) — `fileHash`/`projectedHash` compared against the current on-disk hash before\n    every real write.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ02802E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002N",
    "text": "A live end-to-end pass through the actual running service/CLI is now underway (a real corpus\nmirror populate via `kg:ingest --track`, followed by real `kg:resolve --create-holder`/`kg:update`/\n`kg:insert`/`kg:remove`/`kg:project` calls against scratch artifacts) — everything in 1-8 above was\noriginally verified only via direct, disk-free calls into each `run*` function against a hand-built\nin-memory `Store`. Items 9-10 are what this pass has caught so far; earlier rounds of the same live\ntesting (recorded only in session history, not here, since they're narrative rather than lasting\ndesign content) also caught and fixed: `kg:insert`'s stdin-detection relying on `isTTY` alone (an\nempty non-interactive read isn't the same as \"nothing piped\"), `kg:update` proceeding silently on\nempty stdin instead of refusing, and `kg:project`'s `writeFileSync` failing on a promoted holder\nfolder whose directory never existed on disk.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ02802E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 14. `kg:ingest`'s confirm/`--force` gate on destructive reconciliation",
    "text": "**Direction, restated.** `kg:project` (graph → disk) is the normal output direction from here on —\nthe whole point of working directly on Apeiron (plan with holders, edit with `kg:insert`/\n`kg:update`, traverse with `kg:tree`/`kg:unfold`) is that a real markdown file is something you\n*produce* at the end, not something every edit has to round-trip through. `kg:ingest` (disk →\ngraph) becomes the secondary, occasional direction: re-absorbing a file that changed on disk for\nreasons outside this graph's own edits (a hand-edit, a `git pull`, a merge). The git hooks\n(`AperasKG/.githooks/pre-commit`/`post-index-change`) currently only call `kg:track`, not\n`kg:ingest` — as this direction becomes the normal one, those hooks need rewriting to match\n(flagged here, not done as part of this round).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Q",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002R",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002W",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002X",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH0KR000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Q:links:Link:00CBHMH0P0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028013",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Q:links:Link:00CBHMH0P0000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0P0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "632"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002Q",
    "text": "**The gap this closes.** Reconciliation's only signal for \"this was removed\" is absence from the\nfreshest disk parse — it has no way to distinguish \"genuinely deleted from the markdown\" from \"only\never existed in-graph, via `kg:insert`/`kg:update`, and hasn't been projected to disk yet.\" Found\nlive: inserting a real (non-holder) block directly into an already-real artifact, then running an\nordinary `kg:track`+`kg:ingest` after an unrelated real edit to the same file, silently tombstoned\nthe un-projected block right along with picking up the real edit. The same blind spot applies to\n`ingestFolderTree`'s own structural sweep ([§6](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/6. Bookkeeping gaps found while designing this (all currently real, all need closing)]]>)) — a real Folder/Artifact whose path\ndisappears from a fresh disk walk is tombstoned outright, no confirmation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002R:props:StringProp:00CBHMGYQ0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002R:props:StringProp:00CBHMGYQ0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002R",
    "text": "**The fix: hold back, don't guess.** Neither call site tries to distinguish the two cases (that\nwould mean guessing intent) — instead, any removal either one is about to make is held back\nunless the caller explicitly says to proceed:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002S",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002T",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002V"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002S",
    "text": "`ArtifactNode.ingestFromDisk(force)`: if `reconcileTree` produces a non-empty `tombstones` list\n  and `force` is false, nothing is committed at all for that artifact — no `hydrateFromParsed`, no\n  `applyTombstone`, hashes untouched — and the tombstone previews (`blockId`/`type`/`title`) are\n  returned as `pendingConfirmation` instead. Retried later (with `force: true`, or once confirmed),\n  it recomputes and applies fresh rather than replaying a stale decision.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002T",
    "text": "`ingestFolderTree(store, force)`: same idea for its `stillRemoved` set — a folder about to be\n  tombstoned is left alone (unattached from the fresh tree, but not tombstoned) and its path is\n  returned via `pendingRemovals` instead, when `force` is false. Renames and additions in the same\n  sweep are unaffected — only the removal step itself is gated.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002V",
    "text": "`kg:ingest`'s CLI client (`kgIngest.ts`) collects both kinds of held-back removal from the first\n  response, prints what would be removed (each artifact's node titles, each folder's path), and\n  prompts once — `Are you sure you want to remove these? [yes/NO]`, defaulting to **NO** on\n  anything but an explicit `yes`/`y`. Confirming re-issues the same request with `force: true`;\n  declining leaves everything pending exactly as the first response found it (re-running later,\n  with or without `--force`, sees the same prompt again — nothing is silently lost or silently\n  applied). `--force` on the CLI skips the prompt entirely, for non-interactive/scripted callers\n  (a future hook included) where nothing can answer it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002W",
    "text": "**Follow-up (closed): `kg:track`'s own removal sweep had the identical gap.** `trackAllArtifacts`\n(`apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`) has its own `stillRemoved` sweep — a real `ArtifactNode` whose path\ndisappears from disk, detected independently of `kg:ingest` entirely (a plain `kg:track` triggers\nit). It gets the exact same treatment: a `force` parameter, held back into `pendingRemovals` when\n`!force`, threaded through `runTrack`/the service protocol. `kgTrack.ts`'s CLI prompts exactly like\n`kgIngest.ts` does, with its own `--force`; `kg:ingest --track` folds the same `force` value into\nits nested `runTrack` call (one flag governs every removal the whole invocation can trigger, tracked\nsweep included — `kgIngest.ts`'s own confirmation list now folds in `trackResult.pendingRemovals`\ntoo, so nothing removal-shaped falls through a gap between the two CLIs).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002X",
    "text": "This one *is* live on the current hooks, unlike `kg:ingest` — `AperasKG/.githooks/pre-commit` and\n`post-index-change` both call plain `kg:track` today, unattended, on every commit/index change. A\ndefault-NO interactive prompt there would either hang waiting for stdin or silently leave the\nmirror stale mid-commit — neither acceptable for something that currently just works. Both hooks now\npass `--force` explicitly, preserving today's actual behavior (unconditional removal, same as\nbefore this gate existed) while leaving the *manual* `kg:track` path safe-by-default. This\n`--force` is meant to carry forward as-is once the hooks are rewritten for the `kg:project`-first\ndirection (still not done — the actual rewrite is a separate, larger change than this gate).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Y:links:Link:00CBHMH0PG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBHMH0KR000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Y:links:Link:00CBHMH0PG000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0PG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "718"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "## 15. `kg:track --reverse` — tracking, pointed the other way",
    "text": "**Direction, restated again.** Phase 0's own asymmetry was never \"ingestion is bad\" — it was that\nthe *cheap* bookkeeping half (`kg:track`: does this file exist, has its hash moved) was always safe\nto run automatically (the git hooks do, on every commit), while the *heavy* content half\n(`kg:ingest`: actually parse and reconcile) always stayed a deliberate, explicit, human-invoked\nstep, never run automatically. Phase 1+ keeps that same asymmetry, mirrored: `kg:project` (the new\nheavy half, graph → disk) stays deliberate and explicit, exactly like `kg:ingest` always was — no\nautomatic projection, ever. What *should* run automatically (once the hooks are rewritten to match\nthe new primary direction — flagged in [§14](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/14. `kg:ingest`'s confirm/--force gate on destructive reconciliation]]>), not done here) is the cheap bookkeeping half's own mirror\nimage: not \"has disk changed,\" but \"has the graph changed since disk last caught up.\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Z",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80030",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80034"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Z:links:Link:00CBHMH0PR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028022",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Z:links:Link:00CBHMH0PR000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0PR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "500"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY8002Z",
    "text": "**The mechanism.** A new field, `projectedHash` (`ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` alike), holds the hash\nof the markdown `kg:project` last actually wrote for that node — set only by `kg:project` itself, on\nevery real (non-`--dry-run`) write, alongside its existing bookkeeping. It's deliberately its own\nfield, not a reuse of `ingestedHash`: that one already carries an ingest-direction meaning (`kg:project`\nsets it to mean \"matches disk,\" `kg:update` recomputes it to mean \"graph is ahead of disk,\" per\n[§9](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/9. `kg:update` and `--text-only`]]>)) — overloading it further would blur \"needs re-ingest\" and \"needs re-project\" into one\nambiguous signal instead of two clear ones.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Y",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80030",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80030:props:StringProp:00CBHMGYQG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80030:props:StringProp:00CBHMGYQG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY80030",
    "text": "`kg:track --reverse` (`runReverseTrack`, `kgTrack.ts`) is the read-only report that uses it: for\nevery real (non-tombstoned) `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` with actual content to render\n(`toMarkdown()`/`toReadme()` non-null/non-empty), recompute its hash and compare against\n`projectedHash`. No field is ever written by this pass itself — it only ever reads and reports,\nexactly as cheap and side-effect-free as forward `kg:track`'s own hash comparison is. Three\ncategories, one pass:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Y",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80031",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80032",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80033"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80031",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY80031",
    "text": "**Never projected** — `projectedHash` was never set. The typical case: a holder populated via\n  `kg:insert`/`kg:update` (or promoted by either) but never yet written to disk at all.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80030",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80032",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY80032",
    "text": "**Changed since last projection** — `projectedHash` is set, but the current render no longer\n  matches it (more `kg:insert`/`kg:update`/`kg:remove` edits landed since the last `kg:project`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80030",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80033",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY80033",
    "text": "**Stale on disk** — the reverse of forward-track's own removal detection: an `ArtifactNode`\n  that's tombstoned in-graph, but whose `path` still names a file that exists on disk.\n  `kg:project` only ever writes, never deletes, so a graph-side removal never reaches the file on\n  its own; this category exists purely to surface that, not to act on it — deleting the file is left\n  to the human. (Not attempted for `FolderNode`: a removed folder mapping to \"the directory still\n  exists\" isn't as crisp a check — a directory can go on existing for unrelated reasons a single\n  hash comparison can't distinguish — so this category stays `ArtifactNode`-only for now.)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80030",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80034",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80034:links:Link:00CBHMH0Q8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028013",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80034:links:Link:00CBHMH0Q8000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0Q8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "87"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY80034",
    "text": "Nothing here is gated on subtree purity the way `kg:project`'s own **(o)** channel is\n([§6](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/6. Bookkeeping gaps found while designing this (all currently real, all need closing)]]>)) — a holder artifact with real, pure content underneath is exactly a legitimate \"never\nprojected\" candidate (it just hasn't been projected *yet*), and one with impure (holder-containing)\ncontent underneath will simply hit `kg:project`'s own existing purity error the moment projection is\nactually attempted; this report doesn't need to duplicate that check to be useful.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002Y",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80035",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 16. `kg:project`'s own reciprocal gap — it could silently clobber a hand-edited file",
    "text": "**§14's issue, mirrored.** §14 fixed disk clobbering graph: a real disk-driven reconciliation\nsilently destroying in-graph content the file itself never knew about. `kg:project` had the exact\nsame failure mode in the opposite direction — graph clobbering disk. Found live: project a fresh\nartifact, hand-edit the resulting file directly on disk (add a section), then run `kg:project`\nagain with *no graph-side change at all* — it silently overwrote the file back to the stale graph\ncontent, destroying the hand-edit. `runProject`'s write path (`kgProject.ts`) never read the file\nit was about to overwrite; it unconditionally `writeFileSync`'d whatever the graph currently\nrendered. Every intervening real change to that file — a hand-edit, an external tool, a\n`git checkout` of an older revision — was invisible to it and got silently discarded the moment\n`kg:project` ran again, with no warning of any kind.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ028001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80036",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80039"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80036",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80036:props:StringProp:00CBHMGYR0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80036:props:StringProp:00CBHMGYR0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY80036",
    "text": "**The fix.** Before the real write, `runProject` now reads the current file on disk (if it exists)\nand hashes it, comparing against whichever field already means \"the graph's last known disk\ncontent\" for that kind:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80035",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80037",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80038"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80037",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY80037",
    "text": "**`ArtifactNode`: `fileHash`.** Deliberately not `projectedHash` — `fileHash` is refreshed by\n  *both* directions (a real `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` read sets it, and `kg:project`'s own write sets\n  it too, to the exact same value), so it's already \"what disk should currently read as, as far as\n  the graph knows\" regardless of which direction last touched it. This matters for the common case\n  of projecting an artifact that was ingested from real disk and never projected before\n  (`projectedHash` unset, but `fileHash` matches disk exactly) — using `projectedHash` here would\n  have flagged that ordinary case as a false conflict every time. `fileHash` unset entirely, with a\n  file already sitting at the target path, is treated as a conflict too — the graph has never read\n  that path, so any existing content there is as unknown to it as a hand-edit would be.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80036",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80038",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMGY80038",
    "text": "**`FolderNode`: `projectedHash`.** No `fileHash`-equivalent baseline exists for a folder's README\n  (ordinary folder ingestion never hash-tracks it). Unlike the `ArtifactNode` case, an *unset*\n  `projectedHash` here is **not** treated as a conflict even if a README already exists on disk —\n  that's just the ordinary first-projection-of-an-already-ingested-folder case, and flagging it\n  would make every folder's first `kg:project` demand `--force` for no reason. Only a *set*\n  `projectedHash` that no longer matches disk counts as a real conflict. (Narrower than the\n  `ArtifactNode` check for this reason — a known, accepted asymmetry, not an oversight.)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80036",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80039",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80039:links:Link:00CBHMH0QR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CBHMH0KR000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80039:links:Link:00CBHMH0QR000:props:StringProp:00CBHMH0QR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "35"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMGY80039",
    "text": "A conflict holds back exactly like [§14](<[[/Aperas-crud-design.md/# Apeiron Node CRUD — Design/14. `kg:ingest`'s confirm/--force gate on destructive reconciliation]]>)'s gate: nothing is written and no bookkeeping (`.holder`\nclear, hash refresh) is committed — the response instead reports `conflict: true`, `kgProject.ts`'s\nCLI prints what's going on and prompts `Overwrite anyway? [yes/NO]` (default **NO**), confirming\nre-issues the same request with `force: true`, and `--force` on the CLI skips the prompt entirely.\nVerified live: a hand-edit survived a decline, got overwritten on confirmation, and `--force`\napplied with no stdin at all; a real disk-ingested-but-never-projected artifact projected cleanly\nwith no false-positive prompt.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY80035",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH0KR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "holder": true,
    "title": "--force gate on destructive reconciliation",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMGY8002P",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG008",
    "text": "Deep live end-to-end testing against the real running service, real CLI, and the real git-tracked mirror (deliberately exploited while Phase 0's mirror was still disposable, before committing to it) surfaced and fixed several more real bugs beyond the design's own original scope: `kg:insert`'s stdin-detection relying on `isTTY` alone (an empty non-interactive read isn't the same as \"nothing piped\"); `kg:update` proceeding silently on empty stdin instead of refusing; `kg:project`'s `writeFileSync` failing on a promoted holder folder whose directory never existed on disk; and — the most consequential one — `project.ts`'s renderer not being tombstone-aware, silently re-baking a `kg:remove`'d (or otherwise reconciled-away) node's content back into a projected file.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG009",
    "text": "That last finding led to recognizing and closing a whole class of gap, in both directions: **`kg:ingest`/`kg:track` (disk → graph) and `kg:project` (graph → disk) could each silently destroy content the *other* direction doesn't know about** — a disk-driven reconciliation tombstoning un-projected `kg:insert`/`kg:update` content it has no way to distinguish from a genuine on-disk deletion, or a projection clobbering a hand-edited file it never reads before overwriting. Both directions now hold back and require confirmation (`Are you sure you want to remove/overwrite...? [yes/NO]`, default **NO**) or an explicit `--force`, never silent — verified live for real removals, real hand-edits, real confirm/decline/force paths, on both sides. `kg:track --reverse` (new) is the literal reciprocal of `kg:track` itself: a cheap, read-only report of which real artifacts/folders have graph-side content `kg:project` hasn't caught up to yet (never-projected / changed-since-projection / stale-on-disk), keyed off a new `projectedHash` field — the same write-time baseline the clobber-guard above compares against.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG00A",
    "text": "**This is the actual Phase 0 → Phase 1 transition.** `kg:project` (graph → disk) is now the primary, deliberate output direction; `artifacts/*.md` is a *projected artifact*, not the source of truth anymore. `kg:ingest`/`kg:track` (disk → graph) become the secondary, occasional direction — never run automatically for their heavy half, mirroring how `kg:ingest` itself was never automatic even in Phase 0. The git hooks (`AperasKG/.githooks/pre-commit`/`post-index-change`) were rewritten to match, live-tested against the real service: `pre-commit` now unconditionally flushes the graph to the mirror and warns (via `--reverse`) about un-projected drift, instead of scanning staged `artifacts/*.md` files for a disk→graph `kg:track`; `post-index-change` now reloads the graph from the mirror (`kg:reload --discard`) after a reset/checkout, instead of re-running a disk→graph `kg:track` sweep — since `AperasKG/Apeiron/*.jsonld`, not `artifacts/*.md`, is now the primary git-tracked content a git-level operation can change out from under the running service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG00C",
    "text": "**Projection Engines (Phase 1)**: the Human UI (SolidJS read-projection, 'Hover Preview' link mechanism) remains undesigned — of the three modes in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A, mode 1 (Artifact Projection, now covering both `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` — see \"Markdown → Fractal Tree Mapping\" above) is implemented and mode 3 (Agentic Interface) is designed (Phase 0, above); only mode 2 (Human UI) is still untouched. Mode 1 now also writes to disk by default (`kg:project`, `--dry-run` to print instead) rather than print-only, per `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B's \"the DB becomes the source of truth\" model.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG00D",
    "text": "**Assertion skill(s) (Phase 1)**: a loadable `SKILL.md` teaching a coding agent when/how to use the `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI (built in Phase 0, above) — not yet designed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG00E",
    "text": "Phase 2+ skills: ingestion-from-arbitrary-sources, *automated* graph search skill (the manual assertion primitive moved to Phase 0, see below), refactoring/lazy-atomization skill.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ13801G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG00X",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBFDZ138004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Y"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Appendix: `kg:ingest` full-sweep id churn, found while validating ApeironNgn's write path",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00X",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5N8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5NG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG00Z",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Y",
    "type": "list",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG010",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG011",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG012",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG013",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG014"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG010",
    "text": "Historical record — surfaced incidentally while checking ApeironNgn's `kg:track:ngn`/`kg:ingest:ngn` write path against real artifacts for the first time (`Aperas-apeironngn-design.md` §4 rollout); not itself an ApeironNgn defect, but affects how that validation has to be done.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG011",
    "text": "Symptom: running the existing TerminusDB-backed `npm run kg:track && npm run kg:ingest && npm run kg:export` against a working tree where `kg:track` itself reported all 18 artifacts unchanged (`content unchanged`, 0 tracked) still produced a wholesale `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` rewrite (10214 insertions / 7968 deletions across all 1194 blocks), plus smaller diffs on `ArtifactNode.jsonld`/`FolderNode.jsonld`. Every block's and artifact's `@id`/`blockId`/`artifactId` was reassigned a brand-new Snowflake value; `parent`/`children` references were updated consistently to match (self-consistent, not corrupted — a wholesale identity swap, not a structural break).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG012",
    "text": "Not yet root-caused: unclear whether the full, no-path-args `kg:ingest` sweep (`ingestAllArtifacts`) bypasses `reconcile.ts`'s existing-blockId-preserving matcher entirely for this case, or whether reconciliation ran but declined to match every single block for some other reason. `kg:track`'s own content-hash check clearly did fire correctly (0 tracked, 18 skipped unchanged) — whatever re-ingested every artifact's tree anyway did so despite that.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG013",
    "text": "Practical implication: a full, non-path-scoped `kg:ingest` run cannot currently be treated as identity-stable/idempotent even when no artifact content changed, so its raw output isn't usable as a byte-for-byte ground truth for other comparisons — this is what forced using a content/structure-based, id-agnostic comparison instead when validating ApeironNgn's write path against it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH2EG014",
    "text": "Not yet filed as a tracked issue. Flagging here so it isn't lost, and so a future full re-ingest producing a similarly large diff isn't mistaken for an actual content change.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH2EG00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Architecture of Documents: Separation of Concerns & Matrix Workflow",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CBGN19NG000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8002",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800F",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800S"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 1. Concrete Reality: The Mixing Problem",
    "text": "Currently, documents in `AperasKG/artifacts/` are massive mixtures of completely different logical concerns. Looking at actual project files (e.g., `Aperas-crud-design.md` and `Aperas-treeview-design.md`), the writer often mixes everything into a single document and sometimes even the same paragraph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5WR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5WR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8003",
    "text": "No transducer or adapter can automatically untangle this. A single artifact today contains:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8004",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8005",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8006",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8007",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8004",
    "text": "**Core Design:** The actual specification (e.g., `3. Core model: placeholder is a flag`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8005",
    "text": "**Issues & Gaps:** Bugs discovered live during implementation (e.g., `6. Bookkeeping gaps found while designing this`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8006",
    "text": "**History & Status:** Implementation progress and verification records (e.g., `Status: implemented, live-verified against a synthetic graph`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8007",
    "text": "**Discussion & Rationale:** Why something was built a certain way, or rejected (e.g., `12. Considered and rejected`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8008",
    "text": "**Implementation Details:** Notes to self about code structure.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5X8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009:props:StringProp:00CBHMH5X8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "## 2. Block-Based Separation of Concerns",
    "text": "To achieve pure Perata (clean projections for the reader), the storage layer must adopt a **Block-Based Separation of Concerns**. Instead of one mixed file, the Apeiron stores strictly isolated documents (or trees):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800A",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800B",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800C",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800D",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800A",
    "text": "**Design Docs:** Pure architectural specifications, data models, and rules.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800B",
    "text": "**Issue Docs:** Bug reports, architectural gaps, and pending fixes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800C",
    "text": "**History/Status Docs:** What was implemented, when it was verified, and milestones.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800D",
    "text": "**Discussion Docs:** Rejected ideas, motivation, and theoretical context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800E",
    "text": "This guarantees that a reader parsing the \"Design Doc\" sees *only* the design, without needing complex transducers to strip out bug reports and history logs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8009",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 3. The Matrix Topology (Physical vs. Logical)",
    "text": "A rigid physical directory structure inevitably fails because software development requires different lenses at different times (e.g., building a feature vs. fixing a cross-cutting bug). Because all edits happen on the unbounded tree (Apeiron), we optimize physical storage for the **Reader** (stability) and use TreeViews/Freeflow documents for the **Agent** (dynamic tasks).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800G",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800J"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### 3.1 Physical Storage: Concern-Centric",
    "text": "At the file-system layer, artifacts are strictly grouped by concern. This forms the system-wide documentation naturally.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800F",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800H",
    "text": "```text\nartifacts/\n  ├── design/\n  │   ├── crud.md                 (Pure Perata: Architecture, Models, Specs)\n  │   └── treeview.md\n  ├── issues/\n  │   ├── crud.md                 (Bugs, gaps, pending tasks)\n  │   └── network.md\n  ├── history/\n  │   └── crud.md                 (Implementation status, log of changes)\n  └── discussion/\n      └── crud.md                 (Rationale, rejected ideas, unstructured thought)\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800G",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800J:props:StringProp:00CBHMH65R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800J:props:StringProp:00CBHMH65R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "### 3.2 Document-Level Skeletons",
    "text": "To ensure uniformity across the corpus, each concern document should follow a strict top-level heading structure. Standardizing these paths (e.g., `crud/design.md/Data-Model`) allows the agent to reliably address them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800F",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800K",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800N",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Q"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800K:props:StringProp:00CBHMH65R002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800K:props:StringProp:00CBHMH65R003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800K",
    "text": "**`design.md` (The Pure Spec)**: Only normative, current-state architectural facts. No \"I think we should...\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800M"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800M",
    "text": "`# Context`, `# Architecture`, `# Data Model`, `# Workflows`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800N:props:StringProp:00CBHMH660000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800N:props:StringProp:00CBHMH660001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800N",
    "text": "**`issues.md` (The Task Tracker)**: Actionable, resolvable nodes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800P",
    "text": "`# Open Issues`, `# Pending Tasks`, `# Resolved`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Q:props:StringProp:00CBHMH668000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Q:props:StringProp:00CBHMH668001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800Q",
    "text": "**`history.md` (The State and Timeline)**: Chronological or state-based facts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800R"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800R",
    "text": "`# Current Status`, `# Milestones`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 4. The Freeflow Workflow (Scratchpad & Dashboard)",
    "text": "The strict physical isolation of concerns is necessary for long-term health, but it is hostile to the creative process. The Aperas workflow bridges this gap by using a **Freeflow Artifact** in the `discussion/` directory as the active workspace.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800T",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800V",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Z",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8012",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800T",
    "text": "When starting a task, the agent doesn't jump between `design.md` and `issues.md`. They create a freeflow discussion document, which serves two simultaneous purposes:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### 4.1 The Dashboard (Context Assembly)",
    "text": "The top of the freeflow document acts as a control panel. The agent authors structural links to all the formal blocks across the corpus that are relevant to the current task.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800S",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800W",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800X",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Y"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800W",
    "text": "**`discussion/crud-reconciliation-task.md`**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800X",
    "text": "```markdown\n# CRUD Reconciliation Task\n\n## Dashboard\n[Current Architecture](../design/crud.md/Architecture)\n[The Bug Report](../issues/crud.md/Open-Issues/Nowhere-Problem)\n[Status](../history/crud.md/Current-Status)\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800V",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W800Y",
    "text": "*(By linking these, the agent anchors the formal state into their workspace. When unfolded via `TreeView`, it projects all these scattered formal blocks into a single localized lens).*",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### 4.2 The Scratchpad (Freeflow Authoring)",
    "text": "Beneath the dashboard, the agent dumps unstructured, messy thoughts exactly as they do today.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800S",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8010",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8011"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8010",
    "text": "```markdown\n## Brainstorming\nSo the issue happens because the parent node is missing.\nIf we use a placeholder flag on the node, it could reconcile safely...\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Z",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8011",
    "text": "This is pure Apeiron. It is unbounded, unstructured, and safe from strict schema rules. It exists only in the discussion concern.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### 4.3 Crystallization (The Update Loop)",
    "text": "Eventually, the brainstorming yields a concrete decision. The thought *crystallizes* from a messy idea into a formal architectural rule, or a formal task.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800S",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8013",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5W8013",
    "text": "Instead of leaving that crystallized rule buried in the freeflow text, the agent projects it back to the formal block using the CRUD surface:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8012",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5WG000",
    "text": "```bash\n# Push the crystallized rule to the formal design block\nkg:update design/crud.md/Architecture --text \"A placeholder is a flag, not a distinct kind...\"\n\n# Push the resolution status to the formal history block\nkg:update history/crud.md/Current-Status --text \"Resolved Nowhere Problem via placeholder flags.\"\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W8012",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG001:props:StringProp:00CBHMH670000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG001:props:StringProp:00CBHMH670001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "### 4.4 The Resulting Ecosystem",
    "text": "This creates a perfect symbiosis:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5W800S",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG002",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG003",
      "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5WG002",
    "text": "The **Freeflow Document** retains the entire historical journey of the thought process, the rejected ideas, and the dashboard of links that defined the task context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5WG003",
    "text": "The **Formal Documents** (`design.md`, `issues.md`) remain pristine and strictly isolated, containing only the crystallized reality of the system.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CBHMH5WG004",
    "text": "The **Agent** navigates the graph easily, using the freeflow document as a central hub that fans out to the formal specs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CBHMH5WG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  }
]
